<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 62,744 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 62,744 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 62,744 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday compared to 63,220 tonnes in the same period on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Monday	Dec 22</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 8,603	 7,226</p>
<p>    Import cargo		54,141	55,994</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, two are expected to sail and nine are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 30,000	 Al Safa		24/12</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 42,000	 Trade Resolve	25/12</p>
<p>Motor gas		25,000	 Iter		   25/12</p>
<p>Soyoil		    5,360	 Champion Trader    26/12</p>
<p>Gas oil		  40,000	 Ying Song Hu	 26/12</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Bunga Selasih	28/12</p>
<p>Tallow		    3,137	 Alam Karang	  30/12</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
